    "objective": "Use a sharp V-cut to get open and turn the catch into a balanced shot.",
    "setup": "Passer at the top; shooter at the wing.",
    "organization": "Shooter rebounds, passes to the passer line, and joins the other wing.",
    "instructions": [
      "Walk toward the block as if cutting inside.",
      "Plant the inside foot and push hard back toward the wing.",
      "Show the outside hand as the target.",
      "Catch with the feet set (hop or 1-2) and shoot.",
      "Alternate wings."
    ],
    "coachingPoints": [
      "Slow in, fast out.",
      "Plant on the inside foot to change direction.",
      "Hands ready before the catch."
    ],
    "commonMistakes": [
      "Rounding the cut into a lazy loop.",
      "Catching off balance and drifting.",
      "Cutting at the same speed both ways."
    ],
    "safety": "Shooters rebound their own ball only when the lane is clear; nobody stands under the rim while others shoot.",
